description={For $p\in M$, let $\2S (p)$ be the algebra of all smooth functions on neighborhoods of $p$. A derivation at the point $p$ is a linear map \[ D : C^\infty (U) \to \mathbb {R} \] where \( U \) is a neighborhood of \( p \) in \( M \), satisfying the Leibniz rule \[ D(fg) = D(f) g(p) + f(p) D(g) \] for functions $f,g\in C^\infty (U)$},%
descriptionplural={For $p\in M$, let $\2S (p)$ be the algebra of all smooth functions on neighborhoods of $p$. A derivation at the point $p$ is a linear map \[ D : C^\infty (U) \to \mathbb {R} \] where \( U \) is a neighborhood of \( p \) in \( M \), satisfying the Leibniz rule \[ D(fg) = D(f) g(p) + f(p) D(g) \] for functions $f,g\in C^\infty (U)$},%
